    "introduction": "In this fix we will be looking at how to replace the internal battery used to store electrical charge for the device. This will require a Phillips #1 screwdriver, a small plastic tool to remove the LCD screen and to remove the battery.\nGood Luck!",
    "what_you_need": {
        "parts": [
            {
                "text": "CR 1220 Battery",
                "url": "http://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_ss_c_0_15?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=cr%201220%20battery&sprefix=cr%2B1220%2Bbattery%2Caps%2C151&tag=ifixitam-20",
                "affiliate_link": "http://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_ss_c_0_15?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=cr%201220%20battery&sprefix=cr%2B1220%2Bbattery%2Caps%2C151&tag=ifixitam-20",
                "available_on_amazon": "http://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_ss_c_0_15?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=cr%201220%20battery&sprefix=cr%2B1220%2Bbattery%2Caps%2C151&tag=ifixitam-20",
                "view_link": "http://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_ss_c_0_15?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=cr%201220%20battery&sprefix=cr%2B1220%2Bbattery%2Caps%2C151&tag=ifixitam-20"
            }
        ],
